<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">11 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 11 February, from 660 BCE to 1990.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">660 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,685 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Legendary founding of Japan by Emperor Jimmu</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">According to the 8th-century chronicles, Jimmu, said to descend from the sun goddess Amaterasu, became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s first emperor on this day. The legend is commemorated as National Foundation Day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/guo-wei" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guo-wei.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">951 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,075 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Guo Wei seizes the throne and founds the Later Zhou</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guo-wei">Guo Wei</a>, a leading general of the Later Han, declared himself emperor and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/later-zhou">Later Zhou</a>, the last of the Five Dynasties. He had marched on the capital after the young emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-chengyou">Liu Chengyou</a> had his family killed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaifeng">Kaifeng</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guo-wei">Guo Wei</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/later-zhou">Later Zhou</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1144 CE <span class="tih-ago">882 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert of Chester finishes translating an Arabic work on alchemy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The English Arabist Robert of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chester">Chester</a> completed his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> translation of the Liber de compositione alchemiae, generally considered the first Latin translation of an Arabic work on alchemy. The next year he translated al-Khwārizmī's book on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algebra">algebra</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabic-language">Arabic language</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1531">1531 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">495 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">English clergy recognise Henry VIII as head of the Church</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Under threat of prosecution, the Convocation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury">Canterbury</a> acknowledged Henry as Supreme Head of the Church in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> 'as far as the law of Christ allows'. The full break with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> followed by 1534.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1752">1752 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">274 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pennsylvania Hospital, the first in the American colonies, opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benjamin-franklin">Benjamin Franklin</a> and Dr Thomas Bond, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a> Hospital admitted its first patients in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philadelphia">Philadelphia</a>. It was the first hospital in what became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1847">1847 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">179 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Thomas Edison is born in Milan, Ohio</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Edison patented more than 1,000 inventions, including the phonograph and a practical incandescent lamp. His laboratory at Menlo Park pioneered organised industrial research.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1858">1858 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">168 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bernadette Soubirous sees her first vision at Lourdes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The 14-year-old miller's daughter reported seeing a lady in white in the grotto of Massabielle. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lourdes">Lourdes</a> grew into one of the most visited Catholic pilgrimage sites in the world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1929">1929 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">97 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lateran Treaty creates Vatican City</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a>'s government and the Holy See agreed to recognise Vatican City as an independent state. The treaty ended the 'Roman Question' that had divided Church and Italian state since 1870.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1990">1990 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">36 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nelson Mandela walks free after 27 years in prison</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mandela left Victor Verster Prison near Paarl hand in hand with his wife Winnie, watched by millions on television. Four years later he was elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s first Black president.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li></ol>
